{"name":"Big Fish","hex":"#99a38e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"big fish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An important person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big_fish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Big Fish","blocks":[{"text":"Big Fish is a 2003 American fantasy drama film directed by Tim Burton. It is based on the 1998 novel Big Fish: A Novel of Mythic Proportions by Daniel Wallace. The film stars Ewan McGregor, Albert Finney, Billy Crudup, Jessica Lange, Helena Bonham Carter, Alison Lohman, Robert Guillaume, Marion Cotillard, Steve Buscemi, and Danny DeVito. It tells the story of a frustrated son who tries to distinguish fact from fiction in the life of his father, a teller of tall tales."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/41/Big_Fish_movie_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Fish"},{"title":"Big Fish (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Big Fish is a musical with music and lyrics by Andrew Lippa and book by John August. It is based on Daniel Wallace's 1998 novel, Big Fish: A Novel of Mythic Proportions, and the 2003 film Big Fish written by John August and directed by Tim Burton."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Big_Fish_playbill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Fish_(musical)"},{"title":"Fish","blocks":[{"text":"A fish is an aquatic, anamniotic, gill-bearing vertebrate animal with a tough cranium to protect the brain, but lacking limbs with digits. Fish can be grouped into the more basal jawless fish and the more common jawed fish, the latter including all living cartilaginous and bony fish, as well as the extinct placoderms and acanthodians. Tetrapods are descended from fish, so in a break from the long tradition of grouping all fish into a single class (Pisces), modern phylogenetics views fish as a paraphyletic group that includes all vertebrates except tetrapods. To treat fish as a monophyletic group, one would have to classify tetrapods as a clade/subgroup of specialized fish, which would make \"fish\" and \"vertebrates\" synonyms. In English, the plural of \"fish\" is fish when referring to individuals and fishes when referring to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Tim_Burton_Frankenweenie_2012_3.jpg/500px-Tim_Burton_Frankenweenie_2012_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Tim_Burton_Frankenweenie_2012_3.jpg/500px-Tim_Burton_Frankenweenie_2012_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Director Tim Burton, pictured in 2012","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATim_Burton_Frankenweenie_2012_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Helena_Bonham_Carter_2011_AA.jpg/500px-Helena_Bonham_Carter_2011_AA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Helena_Bonham_Carter_2011_AA.jpg/1280px-Helena_Bonham_Carter_2011_AA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Helena_Bonham_Carter_2011_AA.jpg/500px-Helena_Bonham_Carter_2011_AA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHelena_Bonham_Carter_2011_AA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikim